{number: 38}
{title: When the Roll is Called Up}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] When the trumpet of the Lord shall sound, and time shall be no more,
And the morning breaks, eternal, bright and [G7] fair;
When the [C] saved of earth shall gather over on the other shore,
And the [C] roll is called up [G7] yonder, I'll be [C] there.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
When the [C] roll is called up yonder,
When the [G7] roll is called up yonder,
When the [C] roll is called up [F] yonder,
When the [C] roll is called up [G7] yonder, I'll be [C] there.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
On [C] that bright and cloudless morning when the dead in Christ shall rise,
And the glory of His resurrection [G7] share;
When His [C] chosen ones shall gather to their home beyond the skies,
And the [C] roll is called up [G7] yonder, I'll be [C] there.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
Let [C] us labor for the Master from the dawn till setting sun,
Let us talk of all His wondrous love and [G7] care;
Then when [C] all of life is over, and our work on earth is done,
And the [C] roll is called up [G7] yonder, I'll be [C] there.
{end_of_verse}
